      "id": "frame-0",
      "url": "https://jobs.polymer.co/lendica/41094#apply",
      "text": "Daylit (Formerly Lendica) Subscribe Subscribe to updates View jobs Subscribe to updates Enter an email address to receive updates whenever we post new job openings. Email address Subscribe Cancel Confirm your email Check your inbox for an email containing a link to activate your subscription. Dismiss You're now subscribed We'll let you know whenever we post a new opening on our job board. Dismiss Back to all jobs Full Stack AI Engineer Co-Op (Northeastern Students only) Spring 2027 Full-time Boston, MA 20 USD an hour AboutDaylit is a leading AI agent platform for accounts receivable. Our platform automates the manual work of collecting and reconciling invoices so finance teams can scale credit and collections teams without adding headcount. Our customers trust Daylit to deliver a complete view of portfolio health — surfacing at-risk accounts, predicting payment timing, and powering accurate cash flow forecasts. Companies with high invoice volume use Daylit to reduce DSO, eliminate repetitive work, and know exactly when cash will hit the bank.The RoleWe are looking for a Full Stack AI Engineer Co-op to help design and scale our AI-powered finance products. You’ll work closely with engineering and product teams to build new features, optimize APIs, and support machine learning workflows. This is a hands-on opportunity to develop in both backend and frontend systems within a high-growth fintech startup.What You’ll DoDevelop and enhance full-stack applications (Python/Django, React).Collaborate on AI-driven financial tools and APIs.Contribute to database optimization and performance tuning.Participate in code reviews and agile sprint planning.What We’re Looking ForExperience with Python and JavaScript (React preferred).Familiarity with SQL and backend frameworks.Interest in AI, fintech, and applied data science.Strong problem-solving and teamwork skills. Posted September 8, 2026 Tell a friend Share on LinkedIn Share on X Apply now Apply hereName(required) Email address(required) Phone number Location Resume(required)Attach resume/CVAre you legally authorized to work for any employer in the US? (required)selectDo you now, or will you ever require employment sponsorship to work in the US?(required)selectDid someone refer you to this job at Daylit? Please provide their name(required) Submit applicationThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google Privacy Policy and Terms of Service apply. Powered by Polymer Polymer is the leading hiring platform and applicant tracking system for growing businesses.",
